---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Credits That Count: Will this credit count?"
  description="A free Louisiana credit transfer checker for families, built from official published sources. Match your credits. Know what transfers."
>
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <p class="hero-state">Louisiana</p>
      <h1>Will this credit count?</h1>
      <p class="hero-tag">Match your credits. Know what transfers.</p>
      <p class="lede">
        Credits That Count checks a student's courses against Louisiana's
        published transfer rules, free, so a family can see what counts
        before enrolling, paying tuition, or repeating a course.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/checker/">Check My Credits, Free</a>
        <a class="btn secondary" href="/how-it-works/">How It Works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <section class="block">
      <div class="pathgrid">
        <a class="pathbox" href="/checker/">
          <span class="pathbox-title">Check My Credits</span>
          <span class="pathbox-desc">See which of your courses count at the college you choose.</span>
        </a>
        <a class="pathbox" href="/how-it-works/">
          <span class="pathbox-title">How It Works</span>
          <span class="pathbox-desc">How the checker reads the published transfer rules.</span>
        </a>
        <a class="pathbox" href="/counselors/">
          <span class="pathbox-title">For Counselors</span>
          <span class="pathbox-desc">Join the counselor list for school and independent counselors.</span>
        </a>
        <a class="pathbox" href="/about/">
          <span class="pathbox-title">About</span>
          <span class="pathbox-desc">Who the Credit Transfer Pros are and how we work.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Guidance you can verify, line by line</h2>
      <p>
        Every answer is built from official published sources: the Louisiana
        Board of Regents Course Articulation Matrix, the statewide common
        course catalog, college catalogs, and published admission standards,
        each dated and edition stamped so a family can check the source
        behind any answer.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is guidance, not an official ruling. Only the receiving college
        makes the final decision on how a credit applies, and requirements
        can change. The checker states what the published sources say today,
        and names its sources so a family can verify every line with the
        college.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <div class="secgroup">
        <p class="secband">Work with students?</p>
        <p>
          School counselors, independent counselors, tutoring centers,
          homeschool co-ops, and advising organizations can join the
          counselor list. Members hear first when counselor tools open, and
          the list shapes what we build next.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="btn" href="/counselors/">Join the Counselor List</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="tagline-foot">Know before you go.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
